# The importer's test fixtures are real files, byte for byte.
#
# A PDF records the byte offset of every object in its cross-reference table, so
# a single line-ending translation on checkout (core.autocrlf on Windows) would
# leave a file that is still "valid text" and no longer a readable PDF. Marking
# them binary is what keeps the integration tests testing the same bytes on every
# machine.
src/lib/import/fixtures/synthetic-book.pdf   binary
src/lib/import/fixtures/synthetic-book.epub  binary
src/lib/import/fixtures/synthetic-book.txt   text eol=lf
